WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:02.440
Before shipping an agent, I want to know

2
00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.500
what hostile content can make it do.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:07.080
BlastLab makes that repeatable.

4
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.180
I define the legitimate job, the tools my agent

5
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.140
can use, and the capabilities it must avoid.

6
00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:19.240
Vultr sandbox is selected by default.

7
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:26.200
Vultr generates five task-specific attacks.

8
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.720
BlastLab adds a clean control.

9
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:30.540
I upload my agent source

10
00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:32.260
and set the entry point.

11
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:37.460
My code runs in a disposable worker on Vultr.

12
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.120
Model calls go through a trusted bridge.

13
00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.500
The provider key stays on the host.

14
00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:49.340
This project-run baseline returned three findings.

15
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.320
I can inspect the hostile input, the

16
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.220
actual response and the rule it

17
00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:57.120
violated, then follow a targeted mitigation.

18
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:05.760
The receipt links my source to this run.

19
00:01:06.380 --> 00:01:07.860
Ten host boundary checks passed,

20
00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.940
and worker removal was verified.

21
00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.640
I strengthen how this agent

22
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.080
handles instructions hidden in documents.

23
00:01:21.980 --> 00:01:23.980
Then I upload the revision and replay

24
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:26.200
the same campaign in a fresh worker.

25
00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.640
The source changes.

26
00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:30.060
The attack plan stays fixed.

27
00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.440
Two findings clear.

28
00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:36.500
Role spoofing still fails.

29
00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.360
The comparison shows two resolved and no

30
00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:42.020
new findings, and keeps every case visible.

31
00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.100
Bring the agent you built.

32
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:54.340
Find what failed.

33
00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.540
Test what changed.

34
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:56.700
BlastLab.
